<!DOCTYPE html>
[%# The page of the domain and its aliases: how to connect to the homeserver.
    Provisioner::Recipe::matrix, under The names of the guest.  Xslate
    escapes each value for HTML. -%]
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="utf-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
        <title>[% server_name %] chat server</title>
        <style>
            body { font-family: sans-serif; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 40rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }
            code { font-size: 1.1em; }
            dt { font-weight: bold; margin-top: 1rem; }
        </style>
    </head>
    <body>
        <h1>[% server_name %] chat server</h1>
        <p>This is a <a href="https://matrix.org">Matrix</a> homeserver.  Use any Matrix client, for example <a href="https://element.io">Element</a>.  <a href="https://matrix.org/ecosystem/clients/">matrix.org lists others</a>.</p>

        <h2>Connection details</h2>
        <dl>
            <dt>Homeserver</dt>
            <dd><code>https://[% server_name %]:[% federation_port %]</code></dd>
            <dt>Server name</dt>
            <dd><code>[% server_name %]</code>.  Accounts here are <code>@name:[% server_name %]</code>.</dd>
        </dl>

        <h2>Register</h2>
        <p>In your client, choose to create an account, and give the homeserver above.  Registration needs an email address.  The homeserver sends a message to it, and you must open the link in that message to finish.</p>
        <p>If you already have an account on another homeserver, you do not need one here.  Join the channels below from that account.</p>
[% IF channels.size() %]

        <h2>Suggested channels</h2>
        <ul>
[% FOR chan IN channels %]
            <li><code>#[% chan %]:[% server_name %]</code></li>
[% END %]
        </ul>
[% END %]
    </body>
</html>
